            {"id": "a", "text": "SATA data cable paired with a SATA power connector", "correct": True, "rationale": "Correct. Modern optical drives use the same SATA interface as hard drives. The SATA data connector is a 7-pin L-shaped (keyed) connector, and the SATA power connector is a 15-pin L-shaped keyed connector. They are separate but often described together as the SATA cable assembly for optical drives."},
            {"id": "b", "text": "Molex 4-pin power plus 40-pin IDE ribbon data cable", "correct": False, "rationale": "Incorrect. Older PATA/IDE optical drives used a 40-pin ribbon cable for data and a 4-pin Molex connector for power. Modern drives use SATA. The description of 'L-shaped notch' matches SATA, not IDE."},
