            {"id": "c", "text": "The M.2 2280 length limits sequential performance to 550 MB/s", "correct": False, "rationale": "Incorrect. '2280' refers to module dimensions (22 mm wide, 80 mm long). Physical length has no bearing on protocol speed. NVMe M.2 2280 drives achieve multi-GB/s speeds."},
            {"id": "d", "text": "BIOS must have Secure Boot disabled for NVMe performance to be unlocked", "correct": False, "rationale": "Incorrect. Secure Boot is a firmware security feature that validates OS bootloaders; it does not affect storage device throughput or protocol selection."},
