            {"id": "d", "text": "Use a step-down transformer to convert 230V to 120V before the PSU", "correct": False, "rationale": "Incorrect. A step-down transformer is unnecessary for a full-range PSU that already accepts 100–240V input. Using a transformer would be wasteful, add bulk, and introduce additional failure points without benefit."},
